  "reasoning": "The 2026 U.S. Senate race in South Dakota features incumbent Republican Sen. Mike Rounds against Democrat Julian Beaudion and independent Brian Bengs, with Rounds easily dispatching a primary challenge and no evidence of competitive general-election polling to date.[3][7][16] The state\u2019s statewide Cook Partisan Voting Index is R+15, indicating a strong structural Republican advantage that aligns with recent statewide results and current registration data showing Republicans outnumber Democrats by roughly 2.5:1.[1][8][10] With the governor\u2019s race rated solidly Republican by Cook and GOP registration hitting an all-time high, the lack of head-to-head polling plus these fundamentals point to a very strong Republican edge; in the absence of current general-election polling, the best available margin proxy is the R+15 statewide PVI and prior federal results, so the current_margin is reported as an estimated 15-point Republican advantage rather than a measured poll spread.[1][11][15]",
